text:
*The evening hangs beneath the moon, * 

 *A silver thread on darkened dune. * 

 & nbsp; 

 Fall was not a good season, and for once the music did n't help. Alex was absentmindedly typing a poem when he started to feel it. It was a queasy feeling that started in his chest and worked its way through his veins. Usually he just put on the music and it went away. He listened closer to the next verse: 

 & nbsp; 

 *With closing eyes and resting head* 

 *I know that sleep is coming soon* 

 & nbsp; 

 Alex's breathing became heavier as he closed his eyes. When he opened them, he glued his eyes on the YouTube video that played his music. It had always been his favorite piece, but now it sent a different kind of shivers down his spine. It was a capella, but it filled up the space of his mind as if it were a wall of sound. 

 & nbsp; 

 *Up on my pillow safe in bed* 

 *A thousand pictures fill my head* 

 & nbsp; 

 The song reminded him too much of Persephone. God, she was beautiful. She used to have long, curly hair the color of charcoal, and deep brown eyes. She was smaller than Alex, but their hands locked perfectly. 

 The queasy feeling was only going to get worse. 

 & nbsp; 

 *I can not sleep, my mind's aflight* 

 *And yet my limbs seem made of lead. * 

 & nbsp; 

 Alex paused the video and the space filled the room. It's a sad day when poetry is too real. Alex could n't stop thinking about Persephone. That's how young love is. As the silence got louder, Alex's mind raced, thinking about every little detail. The white dress she wore to every date. The little silver ring that he gave her on their anniversary. The frailty with which she stood up. 

 It had been three autumns since their first date. The first was perfect. The second was when she started moving a little slower. The third... 

 Alex brought his fingers down on the space bar. 

 & nbsp; 

 *If there are voices in the night, * 

 *A frightening shadow, flickering light* 

 & nbsp; 

 The harmonies fell onto him hard. Her last words were `` I love you'', and they were spoken quietly and breathily. It was a dark ER room, and it was a cloudy day outside. 

 & nbsp; 

 *Then I surrender unto sleep* 

 *Where clouds of dream 

 *Give second sight* 

 & nbsp; 

 Even when she passed away she was smiling. 

 & nbsp; 

 *What dreams may come, both dark and deep* 

 *Of flying wings and soaring leap* 

 *As I surrender unto sleep* 

 *As I surrender unto sleep* 

 *As I surrender unto sleep* 

 & nbsp; 

 Alex would survive. But love comes in seasons. There's the spring and summer where everything is beautiful. But this autumn Alex needed to cry. Of course he would find someone else, but for now he needed to sleep. 

 & nbsp; 

 ( ( Thanks for listening. The song referenced in this prompt is Eric Whitacre's `` Sleep''. The poetry is by Charles Anthony Silvestri. ) )
